      "problem": "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{x+5}}{\\sqrt{x-4}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator.",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{x-4}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{x-4}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+5}}{\\sqrt{x-4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+5}}{\\sqrt{x-4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x-4}}{\\sqrt{x-4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+5}\\cdot \\sqrt{x-4}}{(\\sqrt{x-4})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{(x+5)(x-4)}}{x-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+x-20}}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
